hint-select = Click a face to select its occurrence. Shift-click adds. Middle-drag or right-drag to orbit, wheel to zoom.
hint-line = Line is not available in this stage.
hint-rectangle = Click the first corner, then the opposite one. Or type “3000,2000” + Enter for an exact rectangle.
hint-circle = Click the centre, then a radius point. Endpoints and existing circle centres snap; type a radius + Enter for an exact circle.
hint-arc = Click start, end, then a bulge point. Endpoints, midpoints, circle centres and tangent points snap; type the exact bulge + Enter.
hint-cut-through = Draw a rectangle strictly inside the selected top face. The cut passes through the complete solid; type width,depth for an exact opening.
hint-pocket = Draw a rectangle strictly inside the selected top face. After the profile preview, type the blind depth and press Enter to commit.
hint-revolve = Select a closed profile, click two points for its in-plane axis, then type an exact angle from 0° through 360°.
hint-planar-offset = Select a standalone rectangular profile, enter a signed exact offset distance, then press Enter. Preview never changes the document.
hint-sweep = Select a bounded rectangular profile with its straight open path, inspect the exact preview, then press Enter. Preview never changes the document.
hint-loft = Select 2–16 bounded spline profiles in increasing elevation order, inspect the exact preview, then press Enter. Preview never changes the document.
hint-shell = Select the stable top face, enter exact wall thickness, then press Enter. Preview never changes the document.
hint-fillet = Select the stable top-east edge midpoint, enter the exact radius, then press Enter.
hint-chamfer = Select the stable top-east edge midpoint, enter the exact distance, then press Enter.
hint-solid-subtract = Click the target solid, then the cutting tool. Hold Ctrl on the tool click to keep it; Enter commits one undo step.
hint-solid-union = Click the target solid, then the solid to join. Hold Ctrl on the tool click to keep it; Enter commits one undo step.
hint-solid-intersect = Click the target solid, then the overlapping solid. Hold Ctrl on the tool click to keep it; Enter commits the exact common volume in one undo step.
hint-solid-split = Click the target solid, then a boundary-crossing splitter. The splitter is always preserved; Enter commits the exact partition in one undo step.
hint-push-pull = Hover a face and drag along its highlighted normal. Positive distance pushes outward; negative pulls inward. Values are millimetres.
hint-move = Drag an occurrence, or click it and then click its destination. Hold Ctrl at the first press to copy; Shift constrains the dominant axis. Ctrl+C and Ctrl+V also copy and paste the selection.
hint-measure = Click the first point, then the second one. The distance is a reading only — it never changes the model. Esc clears it.
hint-orbit = Drag to orbit. Wheel to zoom, Shift+middle-drag to pan.
hint-pan = Drag to pan the view.
